      "math_academy_id": "e-12753",
      "problem": "Express the following statement in formal language:\n\nThere is a prime $p$ that is even.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate we use an existential quantifier, $\\exists.$\n\n- The sentence refers to the prime numbers. So, by denoting a prime number as $p,$ we have that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14254548/assets/25b45ded54c9020455c1a9590c76c3abb5e18871d41b576b6e06bc21cc2270b3.svg)\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as\n\n$$\np \\textrm{ is even.}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\\exists$ $p$ prime, $p$ is even.\n\nWe could also write\n\n$\\exists$ $p$ prime, $2\\mid p.$",
